    {
      "id": "note-overview",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -680,
        "y": -300
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Vaswani et al., \"Attention is all you need\" (NeurIPS 2017): self-attention lets every position read every other one in a single step, with no recurrence. Sorting is a clean test of that, since each output slot depends on the whole input. Recipe: 5000 random sequences of 10 digits and their sorted versions, Embedding, sinusoidal PositionalEncoding, a 2-layer TransformerEncoder (d_model 64, 4 heads), a Linear head over the 10 digits, LMCrossEntropyLoss, Adam at lr 0.001, 20 epochs. With seed 0 on a CPU it sorts 1000 fresh sequences with exact-match accuracy 1.00 and per-position accuracy 1.000.\n\nVaswani 等人，〈Attention is all you need〉（NeurIPS 2017）：自注意力讓每個位置一步就能讀到其他所有位置，不需要遞迴。排序很適合檢驗這一點，因為每個輸出位置都取決於整個輸入。配方：5000 條隨機的 10 位數字序列和排序後的版本，Embedding、正弦 PositionalEncoding、2 層 TransformerEncoder（d_model 64、4 個 head），Linear 輸出 10 個數字的分數，LMCrossEntropyLoss，Adam、lr 0.001，20 個 epoch。seed 0、用 CPU 跑，在 1000 條沒看過的新序列上，整條完全排對的比例是 1.00，逐位置的準確率是 1.000。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "start",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": -420,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 360
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-data",
      "type": "note",
